# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Re-clone at build time; the working tree under sources/uv/ is gitignored.
#
# TOOLCHAIN SOURCE — a tool this repo actually RUNS (#81, ingested 2026-08-02).
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the version we actually run.
#   version source: mise.toml `[tools] uv`
#   pinned here:    0.12.5
# Cross-checkable without trusting this file: `uv --version` prints the tag's own
# short commit (`210d1f678`), so binary and pin verify against each other — the
# same property ty has and ruff does not.
#
# ⚠️ ASK `mise exec -- uv`, NOT bare `uv`. Measured 2026-08-19 right here: bare
# `uv --version` reported 0.12.3 (507230998) while `mise exec -- uv --version`
# reported 0.12.5 (210d1f678) — `command -v uv` resolves into the OLD install
# dir, which stays on PATH after a bump. The pin was correct and installed the
# whole time; only the shell was stale. A cross-check run through the wrong uv
# reports a drift that does not exist, which is worse than not checking.
# A pin that drifts from the installed version makes the corpus answer questions
# about code we are not running. Not hypothetical — `sources/graphify.manifest`
# records exactly that failure: it sat two releases behind for weeks, so every
# "how does graphify work?" answer came from the wrong source.
#
# Pin the RELEASE TAG, never a branch head — a branch drifts ahead of the release.
# To bump: change the version in its source above, then
#   git ls-remote --tags --refs https://github.com/astral-sh/uv | grep <version>
# and set ref/commit here to match, then `mise run kb-build`.
#
# kind = code: AST extraction only, no LLM, no cost. NOTE this extracts the
# SOURCE and skips every .md by design — the tool's DOCS are a separate
# `kind = docs` mirror (#123), not this manifest.
url = https://github.com/astral-sh/uv
ref = 0.12.7
commit = 61291a8ca5477a9ca653f14d2ac5665587c263fa
kind = code
added = 2026-08-02
